# Flutter Base Production — Cursor

Use Agent mode for material work and index the repository before planning.
Read `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/REUSABLE_COMPONENT_CATALOG.md`, and relevant
current docs. `.cursor/reference/` and `.claude/reference/` are historical,
non-binding material.

- Inspect before editing and plan before a multi-file change.
- Preserve Clean Architecture, BLoC/Cubit, routing/DI, flavors, localization,
  canonical widgets, compatibility adapters, tests, and optional-package
  isolation.
- Reuse `AppButton`, `DefaultTextField`, `AppDropdown`, `AppStateView`,
  `AppMedia`, `AppImagePickerField`, `AppPageShell`, standard feedback,
  `AsyncBlocBuilder`, and `PaginatedListWidget` before adding variants.
- Keep notifications, Remote Config, Maps, WebView, sockets, analytics, and
  crash providers in optional packages.
- Keep Android/iOS IDs, flavors, names, icons, native splash, Maps/Firebase
  sources, signing, links, APNs, and store preparation in parity. Run
  `scripts/check_project_identity.sh` after native/identity changes.
- Never invent APIs, fields, keys, credentials, tool access, device/Figma runs,
  or command results. Never expose raw backend/plugin errors or sensitive logs.
- Make file-scoped changes and verify them in the terminal. Test failure,
  cancellation, concurrency, lifecycle, AR/EN, RTL/LTR, themes, accessibility,
  debug, and release as applicable.
- Do not run Git or destructive operations unless explicitly authorized.

Use `scripts/flutter_quality_gate.sh quick|full|release`; expensive builds are
`release --build`. Use Cursor adapters from `docs/prompts/README.md`. Historical
rules were archived because they duplicated and contradicted the current base.
